  <category name="OnsetRRSampler">
    <reapack name="OnsetRRSampler.jsfx" type="effect" desc="Onset Round-Robin Sampler">
      <metadata>
        <description><![CDATA[{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Onset Round-Robin Sampler\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drop one or more audio files (straight from REAPER's Media Explorer, or from Explorer/Finder) onto the plugin window. Long files containing many one-shots (e.g. 20 footstep variations in one take) are split automatically with onset detection. Incoming MIDI notes then cycle through the detected hits (sequential, random, random-without-repeat or key-mapped).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Companion actions "OnsetRR - Load Media Explorer selection" and "OnsetRR - Append Media Explorer selection" send the files selected in the Media Explorer to the sampler on the selected track (needs js_ReaScriptAPI for reading the Media Explorer selection; falls back to selected items / a file dialog).\par}
}
]]></description>
        <link rel="website">https://github.com/MartinS9001/ReaJSFX</link>
      </metadata>
